<title>FINLAND: NORDIC SKIING-RESULTS OF NORDIC COMBINED WORLD CUP EVENT.</title>
<headline>NORDIC SKIING-RESULTS OF NORDIC COMBINED WORLD CUP EVENT.</headline>
<dateline>LAHTI, Finland 1997-03-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading results in the 90</p>
<p>metre ski-jumping element of a Nordic Combined World Cup event</p>
<p>on Saturday.</p>
<p>1. Halldor Skard, Norway, 237 points</p>
<p>2. Hannu Manninen, Finland, 236.5, 3 seconds behind</p>
<p>3. Mario Stecher, Austria, 234.5, 15 seconds behind</p>
<p>4 equal. Samppa Lajunen, Finland, 233.5, 21 seconds behind</p>
<p>4 equal. Valeri Stoljarov, Russia, 233.5, 21 seconds behind</p>
<p>6. Jari Mantila, Finland, 228, 54 seconds behind</p>
<p>7. Tim Tetreault, USA, 227.5, 57 seconds behind</p>
<p>8. Bjarte Engen Vik, Norway, 226.5, 1 minute 03 seconds behind</p>
<p>9. Ludovic Roux, France, 223, 1:24 behind.</p>
<p>The cross-country skiing element follows</p>
<p>Leading final results after the 15-kilometre cross-country</p>
<p>skiing element:</p>
<p>1. Manninen, 42 minutes 02.5 seconds</p>
<p>2. Skard, 44:05.7, 2:00.2 behind</p>
<p>3. Tetreault, 43:45.2, 2:36.7 behind</p>
<p>4. Lajunen, 44:32.8, 2:48.3 behind</p>
<p>5. Kenji Ogiwara, Japan, 43:32.2, 2:56.7 behind</p>
<p>6. Sylvain Guillaume, France, 43:32.4, 3:05.9 behind</p>
<p>7. Vik, 44:15.4, 3:12.9 behind</p>
<p>8. Mantila, 44:32.1, 3:20.6 behind</p>
<p>9. Fabrice Guy, France, 43:47.3, 4:44.8 behind</p>
<p>10. Trond Einar Elden, Norway, 41:41.6, 5:06.3 behind</p>
</text>
